    "name": "Mudassir Khan",
    "body": "the 43% failure rate from a single provider outage is a number I've seen come up in postmortems more than I'd like — the gap between \"we know we're locked to one vendor\" and \"we measure the blast radius\" tends to be about two incidents.  one thing the migration guide doesn't fully surface: semantic cache invalidation when you ship a new system prompt. we had a window of about 48 hours where cached responses from the old instruction set were still returning because the cache key was pure embedding similarity rather than aware of which prompt version generated them. did you add a versioning layer to the cache key, or is invalidation outside Bifrost's scope at this point?  "
